35,2,1,talk,Servas,,"The staffing rolls show most technicians left for industry. Modelling applicants are arriving, though.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,1,talk,Midori,,"Ledgers show vehicle costs frozen, but animal-unit day rates rose sharply after the rebuild.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,1,talk,Kenji,,The spectroscopy suite was idle for eleven weeks. The glasshouse blocks are booked solid.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,Incident logs confirm the spectroscopy delay. Awards on live colonies overran twice as often.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,1,talk,Toshio,,Closeout files show catalogue-style awards still drawing users a decade later. Mechanism ones stalled.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,2,talk,Servas,,"@Midori, if animal rates rose, that hurts projects needing live subjects.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,2,talk,Midori,,"@Servas, exactly. The computing hours are free, but the animal costs are up.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Servas""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,2,talk,Kenji,,"@Benjamin, the idle spectroscopy suite is a major risk for any project needing it.","{""words"":14,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"@Kenji, yes. And the live colony overruns confirm the biological risk is higher.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[""Kenji""],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,2,talk,Toshio,,"@Midori, the free computing hours make simulation-based projects much more attractive.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[""Midori""],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,3,talk,Servas,,"The lack of technicians is a problem, but the modelling staff is growing.","{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,3,talk,Midori,,The cost structure favors projects that don't rely on expensive animal units.,"{""words"":12,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,3,talk,Kenji,,The shared facilities are strained. We need a project that doesn't overload them.,"{""words"":13,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,The data suggests avoiding live breeding colonies and heavy instrumentation dependence.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,3,talk,Toshio,,"The closeout data strongly favors projects that produce lasting, accessible data.","{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
